abstract: >-
  A national addressing model for Cabo Verde: every building has a home code
  made of the short name of its bairro, zona or povoação and a 3- or 4-digit
  number, unique in the country on its own, pointing to the lote's gate or
  front door, beside the Correios postcode, the municipal street address and
  the cadastre. The paper describes the model, its engine and specification,
  the registry of the 175,630 codes issued, and the expected benefits for
  citizens, logistics, emergency services and government.
